      'Hilf al-Fudul: after a Yemeni merchant is cheated, the youth joins the clans’ pact at Abdullah ibn Judan’s house to defend every wronged person — a pledge he honoured even after Islam (“I would not exchange it for red camels”).',
      'Marriage: Khadijah, 40, wealthy twice-widowed merchant, proposes through Nafisa after Maysarah’s glowing report of the Syrian journey (the cloud, the monk Nastura’s words); he is 25. Mahr: twenty young camels. Twenty-five years of faithful, monogamous marriage follow.',
